"The Oracle is a birth transmigrator from Xanathu, a world of toxic surface and buried cities."
"The Oracle remembers much of Xanathu, whose machines worked much like the System, and its chess."
"The Oracle killed a councillor for calling her Astrid, a name from her past, and mused on more."
"The Oracle listens unseen to every council meeting."
"The Oracle sees futures as branching paths, like reading ahead in chess."
"The Oracle cannot change the future directly; she only moves people, who move others."
"She moves Themiel, who moves the Hell Hound Luke, who is meant to move the Nameless Hell Hound."
"The Oracle judges the Nameless Hell Hound able and driven to gain great power."
"The Oracle means the Nameless Hell Hound for an ally, not a captive: friends, not enemies."
"The Oracle holds that every transmigrator has value, and that some may ascend to godhood."
"The Oracle wants transmigrators gathered to her, to steer the world's futures through them."
"The Oracle foresees possible mass destruction across the world."
"The last Oracle tied that coming destruction to the Bloody Peaks."
"The Oracle has seen herself stabbed by many knives, laughing as she accepts it."
"In many of her paths, one close to the Oracle is soon to die."
"The Oracle believes taking Luke may have opened a brighter future, as her visions darkened."
"Each vision costs the Oracle; it grows harder each day to return to her body and the present."
"After a deep search her eyes blaze purple and she freezes, then drinks purple potions to recover."
"The Oracle spends her sight on kings and those near them, never on peasants."
"One of the Oracle's past moves cost the life of Corath, Themiel's closest friend."
"The Umarii who took Luke first learned of a transmigrator in the litter from the Oracle."
